# Goal 7: Fix ilogb/ilogbf — wrong return for zero and subnormals

## Functions
`ilogb` (double), `ilogbf` (float)

## Source Files
- C sources: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/ilogbd.c`, `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/ilogbf.c`
- Rust sources: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathd.rs` (~line 2753), `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathf.rs` (~line 1971)

## Problem
Wrong return values for edge cases:

ilogb (double):
- `ilogb(0.0)`: C returns -2147483647 (INT_MAX-like sentinel), Rust returns -2147483648 (INT_MIN)
- `ilogb(-0.0)`: same issue
- `ilogb(0x0.0000000000001p-1022)` (smallest subnormal): C returns -1074, Rust returns -1075

ilogbf (float):
- `ilogbf(0.0)`: C returns -2147483647, Rust returns -2147483648

The C library uses `FP_ILOGB0 = -2147483647` (INT_MAX negated) for zero, but Rust uses INT_MIN. Also the subnormal exponent calculation is off by one.

## What Needs to Change
Read the C source to identify the exact sentinel values for zero/NaN/infinity and the subnormal exponent calculation. Update the Rust implementation to use the same constants and fix the off-by-one in subnormal handling.

## Success Criteria
- `ilogb(0.0)` returns -2147483647
- `ilogb(-0.0)` returns -2147483647
- `ilogb(0x0.0000000000001p-1022)` returns -1074
- `ilogbf(0.0)` returns -2147483647
- All other ilogb/ilogbf test cases continue to pass
